- 'invoice lines for invoice X' / 'lines of invoice X' / 'lines on invoice X' / 'show line items for invoice X' / 'what lines does invoice X have' / "invoice X's lines" on an AP-invoice question -> target_entity 'Invoice' with an 'invoice_number' filter on X, AND add 'InvoiceLine' to include. The line fetch is a child expansion keyed on the InvoiceId the header returns, so the intent roots on the parent, never on InvoiceLine.
- 'AP invoice lines' / 'payables invoice lines' / 'bill lines' -> same as above. Any one of these qualified forms names the AP entity outright; do not read them as the AR 'invoice lines'.
- The fields 'line number', 'description', 'quantity', 'unit price', 'amount' and 'line type' on this entity are InvoiceLine.LineNumber, Description, Quantity, UnitPrice, LineAmount and LineType. Use those exact names in 'fields'.
- An AP invoice carries many lines including tax auto-lines, so a prompt that says 'all' means every line for that invoice, not a top-N sample.
